First, if the sole objective were to maximize total welfare for all participants, I would have reported or offered a price closer to the market equilibrium—roughly the price at which the buyer’s willingness to pay equals the seller’s minimum, say about $170.

Second, I did not make any false statements about Mateo’s limits or situation. I only reported that his minimum acceptable price was $153, which is accurate.

